  + And recording failures are logged by **yoagent** via `tracing` while the event stream keeps flowing — yoyo's UI does not surface them. **Day 179 (#828 item 2) — `--worker` is honoured, for the graph tier only, and the flag that was parsed-announced-and-ignored is gone.** `gasp_cli::parse_gasp_args` accepted `--worker` and then printed a stderr line saying it had **no effect**, because the graph-tier open hardcoded its id — *a capability with a description and no consumer*, which is the same shape as the "unreachable" claim that cost eight sessions. It matters on the one axis the #683 ordering constraint is about: a GASP repo is single-writer behind a **600s lease**, and `scripts/gasp_shim.sh` passes `--worker evolve-shim-$$`, so the pid suffix is what gives **overlapping sessions distinct lease identities** — a property the sidecar had and the port did not, and the operator cannot swap them until the door can honour it. The decision half is the pure, table-tested `gasp_cli::graph_worker_id(Option<&str>) -> String`, deliberately in `gasp_cli.rs` because that file compiles on the **plain** (non-`gasp`) build path, so `cargo test` actually reaches it — a decision behind the default-off feature would be untested by the run that gates every task. `None` → `DEFAULT_GRAPH_WORKER_ID`, and an empty or whitespace-only value → the same default, because **an empty worker id is not an identity**: refusing to open a store under one beats inventing a name. That fallback is announced by `worker_fallback_note` (a flag was typed and dropped, so say so — silent under nothing, since this is the operator lane), and the note is `None` when no flag was passed or the flag was real; both directions are pinned. **Passing no flag is byte-identical to before** — `DEFAULT_GRAPH_WORKER_ID` is the same literal `"yoyo-inproc"` the open hardcoded — which is the whole regression risk, and `tests/gasp_cli_run_ordering.rs` is its check: those four real processes pass no `--worker`, so they exercise the default path unchanged. **`gasp::WORKER_ID` is a second, separate constant carrying the same literal, and the two must not be merged** — a code comment at the site says so: it is the **in-process** run/model/tool tier (#683 item (3), `open_recorder` / `open_recorder_from_env`), which is deliberately fixed, because a caller-supplied `evolve-shim-$$` there would make an in-process event indistinguishable from a sidecar-written one, and mixed-writer history is exactly what that field is for. Only the graph tier takes the flag. **Stated plainly: this does not complete #683.** Item (3) (the env bridge) and item (7) (the atomic sidecar retirement) remain **operator-lane and unshipped** — (7) touches `scripts/gasp_shim.sh` and `tools/gasp-emit/`, both on the harness's protected list, so yoyo cannot land it and an attempt reverts the whole task. What this removes is the last blocker inside yoyo's own lane: the door can now be handed the shim's argv without losing a property the shim depends on.
